      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Compatible fluorophores or auto-fluorescence settings"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [
    {
      "technique": "Micro-Computed Tomography (micro-CT)",
      "why_useful": "Micro-CT is the standard method for non-destructive 3D visualization and quantification of the internal pore architecture of opaque materials."
    }
  ],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "No instrument in the current list can perform non-destructive 3D internal imaging of opaque porous specimens. Micro-CT is the ideal technique for this requirement but is not available. Multiphoton or confocal microscopy (EQ08, EQ07) are listed as supplementary options, but they only work if the sample is translucent or can be fluorescently labeled, and they are limited by light penetration depth."
}

